# shadcn/ui conventions

## Use primitives first

Import interactive UI from `@/components/ui/` before writing custom buttons, cards, or tabs:

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
```

Add missing components: `vp dlx shadcn@latest add <name>`

## Semantic tokens over hardcoded colors

For layout chrome (backgrounds, text, borders), use theme tokens:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border">
<p className="text-muted-foreground">

// ❌ BAD for generic UI
<div className="bg-stone-50 text-stone-800 border-stone-200">
```

Hardcoded amber/orange/emerald/rose classes are OK for **domain accents** (day colors, canvas cards, sticky notes) — not for nav, buttons, or standard cards.

## Compose with `cn()`

Merge shadcn defaults with one-off layout classes via `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`:

```tsx
<Button variant="outline" size="lg" className="h-auto px-8 py-4">
<Card className={cn("border", item.className)}>
```

## Icons

Use `lucide-react` — matches `components.json` `iconLibrary` setting.

